## Architecture and lifecycle notes

`ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter` is linked only into the macOS provider and harness graphs; Core, the shared native adapter, and iOS products remain independent. Teardown closes the socket, drains socket/signature work, cancels and joins automatic rekey/keepalive tasks, disposes channels, then frees the session. A failed bounded destructor remains visible as failed ownership instead of being reported as closed. Repeated connect/cancel and concurrent close regressions reconcile sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, custom allocations, and buffered bytes to zero.

